From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Gardner <jamestexasgardner@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:25:08 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] devices/fs: let an embedder serve a virtio-fs device
 (DynFileSystem)

The virtio-fs server can only pass through a host directory
(PassthroughFs, PassthroughFsRo) or serve nothing (NullFs). An embedder
that holds its files somewhere other than a host directory - in memory,
in a database, in a content-addressed store - has no way to answer the
guest's FUSE requests itself. krun_fs_add_overlay_file serves a static
read-only buffer, and its FLUSH and FSYNC always succeed, so it cannot
carry a write path or report a write's failure to the guest.

The `FileSystem` trait the server drives cannot be implemented from
outside the crate: `mod filesystem` is private, and the trait has
associated types and generic methods (`read<W>`, `write<R>`,
`readdir<F>`), so it is not object-safe and cannot be stored as
`dyn FileSystem`.

Add `DynFileSystem`, an object-safe trait carrying the FUSE request set
an embedder needs (LOOKUP, GETATTR, SETATTR, MKDIR, UNLINK, RMDIR,
RENAME, OPEN, CREATE, READ, WRITE, FLUSH, FSYNC, RELEASE, STATFS,
OPENDIR, READDIR, RELEASEDIR, ACCESS), with defaults that answer
ENOSYS, plus `DynFs`, an adapter that implements `FileSystem` over an
`Arc<dyn DynFileSystem>` so the existing `Server` dispatches to it
unchanged. READ, WRITE and READDIR pass `&mut dyn io::Write`,
`&mut dyn io::Read` and `&mut dyn FnMut` in place of the generic
parameters.

`FsWorker` gains a `Custom` server variant, selected when the device
carries a backend (`Fs::set_custom_backend`). Errors are Linux errno
values, as for every other server: the guest is Linux.

DAX on macOS: `DynFileSystem::dax_host_addr` returns host memory
holding a file range, which `DynFs::setupmapping` maps into the guest's
window through the existing GpuAddMapping path; `dax_unmapped` returns
it to the backend. On Linux, SETUPMAPPING keeps the trait's default
(ENOSYS): a backend there would hand over a file descriptor to mmap
into the window, which this change does not define.

`filesystem` becomes a public module so embedders can name the request
types (Context, Entry, FsOptions, OpenOptions, SetattrValid, DirEntry).

Signed-off-by: James Gardner <jamestexasgardner@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: jamestexas <18285880+jamestexas@users.noreply.github.com>
